From 057b8026f51d5b2e6676d2f030f67fe81cee8717 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 14:37:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] mcp/cli: support serving a prebuilt app, ASCII-art
 banner, streaming docs

- mcp/loader.py (new): load_app(dotted_path), a uvicorn-style
  "module:attr" loader for an already-built MCPApp, a raw
  fastmcp.FastMCP, or a zero-argument factory returning either.
  Verified against all three shapes plus an end-to-end tool call
  through a loaded raw FastMCP instance.
- cli/commands/mcp.py: `slb mcp serve` now takes an optional APP_PATH
  positional argument. When given, it's loaded via load_app() and
  served directly, bypassing the flag-built MCPConfig entirely; every
  MCPConfig-building flag (--config/--tools/--source/--no-local/
  --no-live/--allow-write/--timeout/--auth-token/--auth-backend/
  --rate-limit) is rejected with a UsageError if passed explicitly
  alongside APP_PATH (checked via click's parameter-source
  introspection, not default-value comparison, so an explicit flag
  that happens to match the default is still caught).
  --transport/--host/--port/--log-level still apply either way.
- mcp/tools.py: expanded ProgressReporter's docstring to explain, with
  a pointer to fastmcp's own source
  (FunctionTool._materialize_generator), why true partial/incremental
  tool *results* aren't possible over MCP - tools/call always delivers
  one CallToolResult at the end, and FastMCP itself collects an async
  generator into a list before returning it. ctx.report_progress
  (already wired up as `stream=True` on glossary_search/
  glossary_get_terms_on) is the closest available thing: interim
  notifications/progress messages while the call is in flight, not a
  change in the final payload.
- cli/banner.py (new): a small verified ASCII-art "SLB glossary"
  banner (plain ASCII, no box-drawing/unicode).
- cli/main.py: BannerGroup (a click.Group subclass) prints the banner
  above `--help`; a custom --version callback prints it above the
  version string, replacing the old click.version_option. Also fixed
  a leftover "MCPApp's" typo in --log-level's help text.

Verified against a real fastmcp 3.4.7 install: load_app() resolves an
MCPApp instance, a factory function, and a raw FastMCP, and the raw
FastMCP case round-trips a real tool call through an in-memory Client.
`slb mcp serve app.main:app --allow-write` correctly rejects with a
UsageError. `--help`/`--version` render the banner correctly.
